## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to implement cross-service consistency guarantees and reason about end-to-end latency under load.

## Key Concepts

- transactional outbox across DB and event bus
- idempotent producers and deduplication
- cache invalidation vs cache warmth
- end-to-end validation under peak load

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-code: transactional outbox pattern
async function commitUpdate(userId, pref) {
  await db.begin();
  await db.run('UPDATE users SET pref=? WHERE id=?', pref, userId);
  await db.run('INSERT INTO outbox (user_id, event_type, payload, processed) VALUES (?,?,?,false)', userId, 'pref_updated', JSON.stringify({pref}));
  await kafkaProducer.send({ topic: 'user.events', key: String(userId), value: JSON.stringify({userId, pref, ts: Date.now()}) });
  await db.commit();
  await cache.invalidate(`user:${userId}:pref`);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test late-arriving events?
- How do you monitor and alert on read-after-write latency violations?

## Why This Is Asked

Test practical tracing and end-to-end visibility across CNPA during retries and regional outages, ensuring the correlation persists across services and layers.

## Key Concepts

- Correlation IDs / distributed tracing across HTTP, DB, Kafka, Redis
- Middleware propagation, headers, and context propagation
- Retry semantics, idempotent writes, and rollback strategies
- Observability: logs, metrics, traces, dashboards

## Code Example

```javascript
// Express middleware to ensure correlation ID propagation
app.use((req, res, next) => {
  const id = req.headers['x-correlation-id'] || uuidv4();
  req.correlationId = id;
  res.setHeader('X-Correlation-Id', id);
  next();
});
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you verify the correlation ID is preserved through PostgreSQL writes and Kafka messages?
- How would you test this under retries and partial outages, including automated end-to-end tests?

## Why This Is Asked

Real-world CNPA stacks face subtle, cross-component bottlenecks during feature flag rollouts. Isolating whether latency comes from cache invalidation, the indexing pipeline, or rollout logic is critical for safe canary deployments.

## Key Concepts

- Outbox pattern and atomic writes across DB and messaging
- Idempotent indexing/upserts in Elasticsearch
- Cache invalidation correctness and TTL strategies
- End-to-end tracing across HTTP, DB, Kafka, Redis, ES
- Canary deployments and feature flag rollout risk controls

## Code Example

```javascript
// Example: idempotent index update for Elasticsearch
async function upsertIndex(docId, doc) {
  // upsert via Elasticsearch; idempotent on duplicates
  await es.update({
    index: 'pricing',
    id: docId,
    body: { doc, doc_as_upsert: true }
  });
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you validate canary rollout safety with metrics and rollback criteria?
- What instrumentation would you add to visualize end-to-end latency across CNPA components in production?

